<!-- TRANSIENT — DELETE THIS FILE ONCE FS.GG.UI.Diagnostics 0.12.0 IS ON THE ORG FEED.

     The #815 instance of the #537 shape the 0.10.0 Canvas/Controls files carried. `apicompat-check.sh`
     baselines off the PUBLISHED feed, so removing a shipped type is a CP0001 break vs 0.11.0 no matter
     what version the tree calls itself — and the `API compatibility gate` is required with
     enforce_admins on (ADR-0103), so without this the 0.12.0 merge cannot happen at all. Once 0.12.0
     publishes, the baseline moves to it, the type is gone from the baseline too, and this suppression
     matches nothing: it is then STALE, and `Issue776StaleSuppressionTests` is what says so. Delete it
     with the release, not later.

     ONE diagnostic, ONE target, and a lifetime — the ADR-0102 shape. NOT
     `ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile`: a blanket file inverts this gate and ships silent breaks under
     a preview-patch, which is the failure `apicompat-publicapi-gate` is registered to prevent
     (ADR-0101).

     `DiagnosticReadinessImpact` shipped in Feature 169 and nothing ever read it — outside its own
     declaration it was named only by the generated surface baselines and by 169's own contract spec,
     and by nothing in FS.GG.Game/.Audio/.Templates/.SDD/.Governance. The concept the contract needed
     was carried by `ReadinessDiagnosticStatus` all along. Dead, not unfinished (#815).

     CP0001 and not CP0002: the whole TYPE goes, so ApiCompat reports the type's disappearance once
     rather than a member-level break per union case. Its nested `Tags` and their fields need no entry
     of their own — they leave with their parent. -->

<Suppressions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0001</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>T:FS.GG.UI.Diagnostics.DiagnosticReadinessImpact</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Diagnostics.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Diagnostics.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
  </Suppression>
</Suppressions>
